# Styling Guidelines

## Tailwind CSS v4 Rules
- Use utility classes for all styling
- Follow mobile-first responsive design approach
- Use semantic class names when grouping utilities
- Prefer Tailwind utilities over custom CSS

## Responsive Design
```tsx
// Mobile-first approach
<div className="w-full md:w-1/2 lg:w-1/3">
  <div className="p-4 sm:p-6 lg:p-8">
    {/* Content */}
  </div>
</div>
```

## shadcn/ui Integration
- Use shadcn/ui components for consistent design
- Install components with: `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add [component]`
- Follow shadcn/ui design tokens and patterns
- Customize through CSS variables in globals.css

## Interactive States
- Implement proper hover/focus states
- Use Tailwind state variants: `hover:`, `focus:`, `active:`
- Ensure keyboard navigation support
- Add loading states with proper visual feedback

## Component Styling Patterns
```tsx
// Button example
<Button 
  className="w-full md:w-auto bg-primary hover:bg-primary/90 
             transition-colors duration-200"
  disabled={isLoading}
>
  {isLoading ? 'Processing...' : 'Generate Image'}
</Button>
```

## Layout Guidelines
- Use CSS Grid and Flexbox through Tailwind
- Implement proper spacing with Tailwind spacing scale
- Ensure responsive design across all devices
- Use consistent padding/margin patterns